---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../config';
import { path } from '../../i18n';
---

<Legal
  lang="en"
  page="deleteAccount"
  title="Delete Account and Data"
  description="How to delete your Tanukonomy account and all your data, from the app and from your device."
>
  <p class="lede">
    Your financial records — wallets, transactions, budgets, freelance projects — are stored only on your own device,
    never sent to any server. Tanukonomy also has an optional account (for signing in with Google); if you created
    one, you can delete it any time using the steps in §3.
  </p>

  <h2>1. How to delete all your data now</h2>
  <p>Pick one:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Uninstall the app.</strong> Long-press the Tanukonomy icon, choose “Uninstall”, and confirm. This
      permanently and immediately deletes every wallet, transaction, budget, and setting.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Clear the app’s data without uninstalling.</strong> Open Android Settings → Apps → Tanukonomy → Storage
      → Clear data (wording varies by Android version). The app stays installed but resets to a freshly-installed
      state.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What data is deleted, and for how long</h2>
  <p>
    Because Tanukonomy has no server, there is no copy of your data anywhere but your device. As soon as you do either
    of the above:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Deleted immediately, with no retention period</strong>: every wallet and its balance, transaction
      history, budgets and their items, freelance projects and hours, and app settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing is kept by us afterward</strong> — we have no way to recover, view, or share data you’ve
      deleted, because we never held a copy of it in the first place.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Your operating system’s own backup (such as Google backup on Android), if you’ve turned it on, is managed by
    Google under their own policies — see <a href={path('privacy', 'en')}>Privacy Policy</a> §4.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Deleting your account (if you have one)</h2>
  <p>
    Tanukonomy has an optional account for signing in with Google — see{' '}
    <a href={path('privacy', 'en')}>Privacy Policy</a> §6. This account is pure identity: there is no sync of your
    wallet/transaction/budget data to a server yet (see §8 of the privacy policy for what's planned).
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>In the app (fastest way):</strong> open Tanukonomy → tap the Account icon on Home → tap "Delete
      Account" → confirm. Your account is deleted immediately; no need to contact us first.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>By email</strong>, if you can't open the app or run into trouble: send a request to the email in §4,
      naming the email you sign in with. We process it within 30 days at the latest.
    </li>
    <li>
      Deleting your account does not delete data stored locally on your device (wallets, transactions, budgets) —
      that data was never sent to your account in the first place. Use the steps in §1 if you want to remove that
      too.
    </li>
    <li>
      Once server-side data sync ships (see §8 of the privacy policy), this page will be updated with the deletion
      timeline for that synced data.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Other questions or requests</h2>
  <p>
    Send them to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Mention your device and, if relevant, roughly
    when you installed Tanukonomy, so we can help faster.
  </p>
</Legal>
